WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Run repository skills in SecondShift
Use skills for release reviews, CI triage, team briefings, and security audits.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Add a skill to your repository
This example uses Cloudflare’s security-audit skill and a small invoice service.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Click Run now
Try the job before you turn on its schedule.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
The manual run starts
SecondShift queues the job against the synced commit.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Check the finding with a sub-agent
A fresh agent checks the same source and repeats the test with demo data.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Read the audit report
The demo showed that Cedar could read an invoice belonging to Maple.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Keep the evidence with the run
Download the report, findings JSON, and coverage ledger.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Enable the cron schedule
Choose a time in the repository manifest. This demo uses a short interval.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:53.000
The next audit runs on schedule
The run shows what started it and keeps its own report.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Reuse files from the previous run
SecondShift gives the next run the saved ledger and findings to review.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.000
File a verified finding in GitHub
The publishing job checks the audit record and files an issue with the autofix label.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Run autofix every night
At midnight, a separate job looks for open issues labeled autofix.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Open a draft PR from the nightly run
SecondShift links the draft to the issue and leaves it for review.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Review the proposed fix
The lookup now checks who owns the invoice before returning it.
